While I like your suggestions here,
I want to challenge the idea that
all roles need to be brought to
parity.

Instead, I think it is A Good Thing
that someone who sets out to ascend
all 13 roles does it well aware that
there are a few real clunkers in the
mix. Where would the challenge lie
in "doing them all", if all roles
were equalized to be exactly as
joyful and as easy/empowered as each
other?

Similarly, when I'm playing roles at
random (just now on the 48th such in
a row), there should be some that
make me smile, and some that make me
groan, else why have more than one?

